            <div xml:id="d952">

                <pb facs="0971" n="859" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg859"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 367116/93.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Ambassador Straus.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1910-06-30"><hi rendition="#italic">June 30,
                        1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 116.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch, No. 173, of the 16th ultimo,
                    concerning the status of the negotiations respecting American educational and
                        <pb facs="0972" n="860" xml:id="pg860"/> missionary institutions in the
                    Ottoman Empire, has been received and read with attention.</p>
                <p>The difficulties with which you are meeting in your efforts to press the
                    negotiations to a successful conclusion are fully understood, and your action in
                    the matter has the approval of the department.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington
                    Wilson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
